We have how many letters of resignation?

104
00:07:37,081 --> 00:07:38,708
Ugh, this is killing me, I can't take it.

105
00:07:39,417 --> 00:07:40,543
He really isn't responding?

106
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:43,629
Oh, hey, I gotta go.

107
00:07:45,715 --> 00:07:47,800
Uh, why are you out here, sir?

108
00:07:51,846 --> 00:07:52,847
You're working hard.

109
00:07:53,764 --> 00:07:55,641
Come on, please, now. Sit down.

110
00:07:55,725 --> 00:07:57,977
I'm going to the toilet. So, why don't you
let me head to men's room?

111
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:04,150
Ah, I'd watch it with the wine, sir.

112
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:08,905
The patients are who we need to worry for,
you sons of bitches.

113
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:12,992
And I hope you all get gout from
stuffing your faces with all that meat.

114
00:08:14,285 --> 00:08:16,162
God, at this point, is there even
a doctor left worth seeing?

115
00:08:18,122 --> 00:08:19,332
Self-centered assholes.

116
00:08:22,376 --> 00:08:24,045
Whoa, this is so awesome.

117
00:08:24,545 --> 00:08:26,756
This is my first time going to the ER
after a manual reduction. Whoa...

118
00:08:27,965 --> 00:08:31,552
You know, I can't say I've seen
something like this either. Weird...

119
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:32,887
Uh, wait! Wait- Wait a second.

120
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:37,225
What's your name?
Can you tell me who you are?

121
00:08:41,187 --> 00:08:42,188
Huh?

122
00:08:42,855 --> 00:08:43,856
What was that?

123
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:45,608
Wait, what's that supposed to mean?

124
00:08:45,691 --> 00:08:47,610
Hey, you didn't say who you are! Hold on!

125
00:08:47,693 --> 00:08:48,694
119 EMS

126
00:08:55,034 --> 00:08:57,537
<i>The White Tower is collapsing.</i>

127
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:03,376
<i>Hospitals nationwide were repeatedly</i>
<i>devastated by the COVID-19 pandemic,</i>

128
00:09:03,459 --> 00:09:06,754
<i>the passing of laws mandating</i>
<i>cameras in operating rooms,</i>

129
00:09:06,837 --> 00:09:09,006
<i>and strikes over</i>
<i>medical school enrollment quotas.</i>

130
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:10,841
DURING CONSTRUCTION,
DEPARTMENTS WILL SHARE A STAFF ROOM

131
00:09:10,925 --> 00:09:13,844
Construction on that started so long ago.

132
00:09:15,805 --> 00:09:17,473
Doesn't seem like
they've gotten anything done.

133
00:09:18,182 --> 00:09:19,183
Ah, shit!

134
00:09:20,142 --> 00:09:23,604
<i>In response, the government proposed</i>
<i>a half-baked, purely symbolic bill,</i>

135
00:09:23,688 --> 00:09:27,650
<i>and doctors responded by</i>
<i>leaving the hospitals in droves.</i>

136
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:30,653
<i>The patients have been</i>
<i>completely sidelined in this fight.</i>

137
00:09:30,736 --> 00:09:33,114
Doctors started it, and now nurses.

138
00:09:33,197 --> 00:09:34,991
It's tough enough being a general surgeon,

139
00:09:35,074 --> 00:09:36,993
how did things things get so messed up?

140
00:09:37,577 --> 00:09:39,078
- I'm sorry, sir.
- Yes, sir, I'm sorry.

141
00:09:39,912 --> 00:09:41,664
I'm making rounds
for the first time in eons, today.

142
00:09:41,747 --> 00:09:44,625
This is humiliating.
And the OR? Who's over there?

143
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:48,963
Well, sir, I...

144
00:09:49,046 --> 00:09:51,340
Given the urgency and timing,
I did call someone in, to...

145
00:09:51,924 --> 00:09:53,676
temporarily assist today.

146
00:09:53,759 --> 00:09:57,096
GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

147
00:10:04,353 --> 00:10:05,354
<i>And...</i>

148
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:08,274
<i>a new kind of doctor entered the arena.</i>

149
00:10:09,358 --> 00:10:11,193
<i>A doctor who belongs to no group.</i>

150
00:10:16,907 --> 00:10:21,829
It's nice to meet you!
I'm your surgical intern, Park Tae-gyeong.

151
00:10:21,912 --> 00:10:22,955
I'm glad to be working with you!

152
00:10:30,254 --> 00:10:31,547
Excuse me, am I late?

153
00:10:32,798 --> 00:10:33,924
Uh, I shouldn't be.

154
00:10:35,676 --> 00:10:37,595
Sir, hi, good morning.
May I please ask you...

155
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:41,891
Morning, how are you? I'm Ma Seong-gyu,
I'm your senior resident.

156
00:10:41,974 --> 00:10:45,269
You'll be valuable to the team,
but I'm too busy to show it,

157
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:48,356
'cause, suddenly, Director Kim
has decided to make the rounds,

158
00:10:48,439 --> 00:10:50,691
which means you're gonna need
to get out there, right now, too.

159
00:10:51,192 --> 00:10:52,234
So, your seat is, umm...

160
00:10:53,402 --> 00:10:54,987
Well, you'll be in surgery,
so it doesn't matter.

161
00:10:55,988 --> 00:10:58,866
You can just, uh... sit wherever. Yeah.

162
00:10:58,949 --> 00:11:00,743
Oh, but that doesn't mean
you should quit this week.

163
00:11:03,245 --> 00:11:05,164
- What are you doing, intern?
- Sorry?

164
00:11:06,123 --> 00:11:06,957
Ah, rounds.

165
00:11:07,041 --> 00:11:08,042
Yes, sir!

166
00:11:14,131 --> 00:11:17,635
<i>Director Kim Myeong-seop</i>
<i>will now begin to make his rounds.</i>

167
00:11:19,512 --> 00:11:23,182
<i>A freelance doctor</i>
<i>unaffiliated with any medical institution,</i>

168
00:11:23,265 --> 00:11:26,102
<i>also known as a mercenary doctor.</i>

169
00:11:26,185 --> 00:11:30,773
<i>This story, at its deepest point,</i>
<i>is the story of the wolf.</i>

170
00:11:30,856 --> 00:11:34,610
<i>A solitary figure who emerged</i>
<i>in the era of the mafia in white,</i>

171
00:11:34,694 --> 00:11:41,200
<i>in which medicine, where life hangs in the</i>
<i>balance, is driven by money and power.</i>

172
00:11:41,283 --> 00:11:43,035
<i>The person that you see before you</i>

173
00:11:43,953 --> 00:11:48,374
<i>flies in the face of authority</i>
<i>and refuses to be bound to anyone.</i>

174
00:11:48,457 --> 00:11:52,294
<i>The only weapons she keeps</i>
<i>in her arsenal are her medical license</i>

175
00:11:52,378 --> 00:11:55,005
<i>and the surgical skills</i>
<i>she sharpened from bare metal.</i>

176
00:11:55,089 --> 00:11:56,590
<i>Gye Su-jeong, general surgeon.</i>

177
00:11:56,674 --> 00:12:00,928
<i>Also known as... Doctor X.</i>

178
00:12:13,107 --> 00:12:15,443
I haven't had a moment to look
through all your paperwork yet.

179
00:12:15,526 --> 00:12:16,861
Your name? First and last.

180
00:12:19,572 --> 00:12:20,656
Gye Su-jeong.

181
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,999
"Gye", you said? That's your name?

182
00:12:33,669 --> 00:12:37,673
Later today, we're holding
a conference to review an operation,

183
00:12:37,757 --> 00:12:39,675
so you should attend that first.

184
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,887
- Hey, you- Wha-
- Ah, Doctor Gye?

185
00:12:42,970 --> 00:12:46,599
When Dr. Do talks to you, you answer.

186
00:12:47,308 --> 00:12:50,352
- Dr. Do, Director Kim's waiting for you..
- Oh, my. Let's go.

187
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:02,323
Wow, looks like Director Kim
is really all in on this surgery.

188
00:13:02,406 --> 00:13:04,241
He's even attending
the conference himself.

189
00:13:04,325 --> 00:13:07,119
Well, given that his retirement
is just around the corner,

190
00:13:07,703 --> 00:13:09,622
I suppose he's pretty excited
he gets to do it.

191
00:13:28,974 --> 00:13:29,809
Please stand.

192
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:31,060
THE 7TH MEDICAL STAFF CONFERENCE

193
00:13:40,736 --> 00:13:41,737
Be seated.

194
00:13:44,990 --> 00:13:47,868
Um... we're ready,
the conference will now begin.

195
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:51,163
The patient is Seo Byeong-gyu,
an 80-year-old male.

196
00:13:51,247 --> 00:13:54,708
Findings suggest gallbladder cancer,
he's scheduled for open cholecystectomy.

197
00:13:54,792 --> 00:13:57,002
At the direct insistence of the patient,
Director Kim Myeong-seop

198
00:13:57,086 --> 00:13:59,880
will serve as the surgeon
and handle the procedure personally.

199
00:14:00,714 --> 00:14:03,133
In light of that, the process that
Director Kim has created and pioneered,

200
00:14:03,217 --> 00:14:05,344
the MS technique, will be applied.

201
00:14:05,427 --> 00:14:08,138
It is a legendary technique
and a surgical standard for 30 years.

202
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:10,641
And this will serve as our opportunity
to witness it in person.

203
00:14:12,518 --> 00:14:14,937
The "MS technique"?
Whatever, it's just open surgery.

204
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:23,153
This operation is likely my last chance
to remind myself that I'm a surgeon.

205
00:14:23,237 --> 00:14:25,364
Don't say that, please, Mister Director!

206
00:14:27,116 --> 00:14:28,450
As I take on this surgery,

207
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:31,704
I will do the best for my patient
and their health.

208
00:14:31,787 --> 00:14:35,791
Allow Dr. Bae and Dr. Ma
to assist you in the operation, Director.

209
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:38,043
I look forward to learning from you.

210
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:40,921
And now, aside from these two,

211
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:43,757
anyone else who is available
should observe it as well.

212
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:45,926
- Thank you very much, Director Kim.
- Thank you very much, Director Kim.

213
00:14:49,388 --> 00:14:50,389
Yeah, I object.

214
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:04,278
Who is that?

215
00:15:04,695 --> 00:15:08,574
Hold on a minute, is that
the temp from the locum tenens agency?

216
00:15:08,657 --> 00:15:10,743
So, is she their ace?

217
00:15:10,826 --> 00:15:12,494
Temp doc? Ace?

218
00:15:13,162 --> 00:15:14,163
- She's...
- What are you talking about?

219
00:15:19,877 --> 00:15:22,212
There you go. Our intern knows what's up.

220
00:15:22,296 --> 00:15:23,797
An ace? Yeah, right.

221
00:15:23,881 --> 00:15:25,591
An "X", more like. An "X".

222
00:15:37,394 --> 00:15:38,604
Is there a reason to go this route?

223
00:15:39,521 --> 00:15:40,522
Do we have to do it open?

224
00:15:41,231 --> 00:15:42,733
Why would you open him up?

225
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:45,778
Laparoscopic cholecystectomy
has long been standard practice

226
00:15:45,861 --> 00:15:48,155
for a durable post-surgery result
and quicker recovery.

227
00:15:48,238 --> 00:15:50,908
If you open him up, the patient
will be hospitalized for at least 10 days,

228
00:15:50,991 --> 00:15:52,534
and it'll be harder on his body.

229
00:15:53,243 --> 00:15:54,828
So why insist on doing it
with greater risk?

230
00:15:56,997 --> 00:15:58,457
Director, I apologize.

231
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:01,251
She's a temp doctor that the hospital
brought in today, she doesn't know what--

232
00:16:03,379 --> 00:16:05,756
I'll grant you this, we rely on
machines a lot these days,

233
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:07,216
and that's all good.

234
00:16:07,299 --> 00:16:10,344
In fact, Doctor Heung-gon is known
for his laparoscopic surgeries,

235
00:16:10,427 --> 00:16:12,179
so he knows better than any other doctor.

236
00:16:12,763 --> 00:16:15,391
Luckily, this case
happens to be very fortunate

237
00:16:15,474 --> 00:16:19,478
as the cancer was detected in this patient
at a routine ultrasound, without symptoms.

238
00:16:19,561 --> 00:16:23,440
However, we're all aware
it's hard to distinguish between

239
00:16:23,524 --> 00:16:26,527
abdominal inflammation
and gallbladder cancer with imaging

240
00:16:26,610 --> 00:16:30,280
when up against the possibility
for cancer to become metastatic,

241
00:16:30,364 --> 00:16:33,409
if we suspect even
the tiniest risk of cancer,

242
00:16:33,492 --> 00:16:35,953
we need surgery to excise all the cancer

243
00:16:36,036 --> 00:16:38,539
instead of relying on
a less invasive approach.

244
00:16:38,622 --> 00:16:40,165
Isn't that right, Doctor Bae?

245
00:16:40,249 --> 00:16:41,250
Yes, Director, that's right.

246
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:45,671
Open surgery has several advantages
compared to a laparoscopic procedure,

247
00:16:45,754 --> 00:16:47,756
in removing the tumors
from the gallbladder and-

248
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,925
As you said,
this is such a fortunate case.

249
00:16:50,634 --> 00:16:52,261
the ultrasound identified
the cancer early,

250
00:16:52,761 --> 00:16:55,180
an early-stage gallbladder cancer
has a high survival rate,

251
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:58,225
so the procedure selected
should factor in the patient's condition.

252
00:16:59,435 --> 00:17:03,439
The patient's 80. He had pneumonia three
years ago from complications of COVID-19.

253
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:05,733
We can remove cancer
with a laparoscopic operation,

254
00:17:05,816 --> 00:17:09,153
send it for biopsy and, based on results,
proceed with open surgery.

255
00:17:09,236 --> 00:17:10,779
She's one smart cookie.

256
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:13,032
That's a call for the surgeon to make!

257
00:17:13,115 --> 00:17:16,410
A surgeon needs the ability to touch
and see the surgical site directly,

258
00:17:16,493 --> 00:17:18,871
so that they can handle
adhesions or bleeding,

259
00:17:18,954 --> 00:17:21,457
remove the disease
at the source, directly,

260
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:25,377
as extensively and deeply as possible,
in order to ensure the patient's safety.

261
00:17:25,461 --> 00:17:28,589
This is the best way,
the most reliable process there is,

262
00:17:28,672 --> 00:17:29,882
to save a life!

263
00:17:29,965 --> 00:17:32,009
- Well said, Director!
- I agree with that.

264
00:17:39,641 --> 00:17:40,642
Looks like...

265
00:17:42,102 --> 00:17:45,272
maybe you're excited because you've been
booked for the first time in decades.

266
00:17:45,355 --> 00:17:46,648
What? "Booked"?

267
00:17:47,858 --> 00:17:50,277
How could you use such
a colloquial word toward the Director?

268
00:17:50,986 --> 00:17:53,822
Oh, instead of "booked", I'll say, uh...

269
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:57,451
Selected by anyone?

270
00:17:58,243 --> 00:17:59,578
"Selected by anyone"?

271
00:17:59,661 --> 00:18:02,039
How dare you speak to Director Kim
as if he's not a legend?

272
00:18:02,956 --> 00:18:04,583
I think you should
be honest about it, sir.

273
00:18:04,666 --> 00:18:06,710
You haven't been selected
by a patient in years,

274
00:18:06,794 --> 00:18:09,213
you wanna operate, but you don't know
how to do the surgery laparoscopically.

275
00:18:09,296 --> 00:18:11,298
Aren't you just
suggesting outdated theories

276
00:18:11,381 --> 00:18:13,592
so you can try and make
your decision sound convincing?

277
00:18:14,635 --> 00:18:19,598
If these people do have medical licenses,
and follow the ethics they're supposed to,

278
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:23,852
they'd likely agree that a laparoscopic
specialist should perform the surgery.

279
00:18:24,394 --> 00:18:27,064
And I bet that laparoscopic specialist
would agree as well.

280
00:18:27,147 --> 00:18:28,690
What was that? I wouldn't say that.

281
00:18:29,399 --> 00:18:31,777
I swear, Director Kim, that's not true,
I don't think that at all.

282
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:34,655
Enough already. Please tell me
what are you trying to do here?

283
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:39,201
What I wanna say, is... uh...

284
00:18:40,828 --> 00:18:42,830
Here, I'll put it less colloquially, then.

285
00:18:44,289 --> 00:18:45,290
Ah!

286
00:18:45,874 --> 00:18:47,084
That'd fit the occasion better.

287
00:18:50,170 --> 00:18:52,589
You are acting greedy... for your age.

288
00:18:52,673 --> 00:18:53,674
Oh, Mister Director...

289
00:18:55,092 --> 00:18:56,260
Get out!

290
00:18:56,343 --> 00:18:57,928
Get her out! What're you waiting for?

291
00:19:03,642 --> 00:19:06,186
Please, sit down.

292
00:19:07,187 --> 00:19:08,522
Oh, my goodness.

293
00:19:08,605 --> 00:19:11,775
Wow. She's extraordinary.

294
00:19:13,652 --> 00:19:16,738
Listen, Miss Jang, that temp
dog of yours you sent me is insane.

295
00:19:16,822 --> 00:19:18,031
Not "dog", "doc"!

296
00:19:18,532 --> 00:19:21,326
She's not a dog, a person, that-
Gye Su-jeong, the surgeon!

297
00:19:22,411 --> 00:19:23,412
What is the matter with her?

298
00:19:24,746 --> 00:19:26,373
My goodness, is that so?

299
00:19:26,915 --> 00:19:29,960
Oh, it certainly seems Doctor Gye Su-jeong
behaved rather inappropriately.

300
00:19:30,043 --> 00:19:31,628
DIRECTOR JANG'S LOCUM TENENS AGENCY

301
00:19:31,712 --> 00:19:34,131
Oh, I'm sorry, forgive me.

302
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:36,550
She can be pretty sharp-tongued.

303
00:19:37,217 --> 00:19:38,760
SU-JEONG, FEB. 9: FIRST DAY AT GUMC

304
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:40,345
Ah. Nonetheless, her surgical skills
are far beyond doubt,

305
00:19:40,846 --> 00:19:42,723
so I'm sure she'll be of
great help to your hospital.

306
00:19:43,348 --> 00:19:45,017
Uh, given everything that happened,

307
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:47,227
I'll give you a discount for the month.
How does that sound?

308
00:19:47,936 --> 00:19:50,564
Yes, of course, I'll ensure she
stays in check now, don't worry.

309
00:19:51,356 --> 00:19:52,357
Uh-huh.

310
00:19:52,983 --> 00:19:54,902
Thank you for working with us.
You take care, now. Mmm.

311
00:19:57,446 --> 00:19:59,072
- I go now, right?
- She caused another issue?

312
00:19:59,573 --> 00:20:01,074
She just said what she had to, that's all.

313
00:20:01,158 --> 00:20:01,992
Ah, here!

314
00:20:02,075 --> 00:20:03,076
Advance one space.

315
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:06,121
Oh. This shoulder hurts,
do some acupuncture, quick.

316
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:08,874
- And will you pay me up front?
- I'll even cook some grub for you.

317
00:20:09,374 --> 00:20:10,709
Grub? Whoa, I'm up for some grub.

318
00:20:10,792 --> 00:20:12,753
- Let's go. One, two, three, four, five.
- No, no... see, I can't let that happen.

319
00:20:17,758 --> 00:20:20,302
Landed on Seoul.

320
00:20:20,385 --> 00:20:22,179
Oh, man. Come on, not Seoul...

321
00:20:24,556 --> 00:20:26,934
When I heard it was gallbladder cancer,
everything froze over.

322
00:20:27,726 --> 00:20:29,144
As if everything around me, just...

323
00:20:29,937 --> 00:20:34,942
After hearing that, I recalled years ago
I saw you on television, talking about it.

324
00:20:35,025 --> 00:20:36,526
And seeing that, I thought to myself,

325
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:40,239
"Gallbladder cancer must be dangerous
if they have this doctor on television."

326
00:20:40,989 --> 00:20:42,157
Oh, yes, that was-

327
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:44,785
Oh, the DBS show, it's the
<i>Secrets of Life and Death:</i>

328
00:20:44,868 --> 00:20:46,912
<i>The Master of Gallbladder Cancer,</i>
<i>Kim Myung-seop Special.</i>

329
00:20:46,995 --> 00:20:48,497
Oh, Director, it's truly an honor for us.

330
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:50,624
As fate would have it, actually,
through my factory,

331
00:20:50,707 --> 00:20:53,961
I've manufactured and supplied gloves
to this hospital for over 20 years.

332
00:20:54,586 --> 00:20:57,506
Of course,
I also supply to other hospitals as well.

333
00:20:57,589 --> 00:20:59,841
But still, I've always taken pride
in supplying to this...

334
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:03,303
- Mm. Please sign this form, here.
- Ah, okay.

335
00:21:03,387 --> 00:21:06,807
- Director Kim has other patients to see.
- So sorry for holding you up. I apologise.

336
00:21:06,890 --> 00:21:08,183
Ah, there's one other thing...

337
00:21:10,185 --> 00:21:14,564
- a small token of our appreciation.
- Oh-ho-ho! So kind.

338
00:21:14,648 --> 00:21:17,276
I could get in trouble
if I were to take that gift.

339
00:21:19,027 --> 00:21:20,737
Oh, please do take it, Director.

340
00:21:20,821 --> 00:21:23,740
Honestly, we just wouldn't feel right
unless we could properly give our thanks.

341
00:21:23,824 --> 00:21:25,200
We insist on it, sir.

342
00:21:25,284 --> 00:21:27,202
Please take our gift, Director Kim.

343
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:31,290
Yes, Director. Thank you very much.

344
00:21:34,042 --> 00:21:35,669
Uh, Director Kim,
the update should be done soon.

345
00:21:35,752 --> 00:21:37,796
Can I help with
anything else you might need?

346
00:21:37,879 --> 00:21:39,172
No.

347
00:21:39,256 --> 00:21:42,050
- Get back to work when it's done.
- Yes, sir, will do.

348
00:21:51,018 --> 00:21:54,187
Good grief. Ugh!

349
00:22:00,485 --> 00:22:01,653
Uh, Director, I'm done with the update.

350
00:22:02,404 --> 00:22:03,405
Get this out of here.

351
00:22:04,072 --> 00:22:06,325
- empty that trash can while you're at it!
- Yes, thank you, we will.

352
00:22:17,294 --> 00:22:18,295
"Thanks for everything."

353
00:22:18,879 --> 00:22:20,255
What did I thank him for?

354
00:22:22,257 --> 00:22:23,383
What do you got?

355
00:22:23,467 --> 00:22:24,468
Ah, it's <i>jocheong, </i>actually.

356
00:22:25,218 --> 00:22:27,471
<i>Jocheong</i>? Okay. That stuff's like honey?

357
00:22:28,513 --> 00:22:31,433
I think it's homemade, with how it looks.
The ones at the store aren't this color.

358
00:22:31,516 --> 00:22:32,726
How do you know all that?

359
00:22:33,727 --> 00:22:36,396
Oh, my grandma'd always make some for me
when I'd go and visit during the holidays.

360
00:22:37,189 --> 00:22:39,983
She made some for me when
I took the CSAT to wish me good luck,

361
00:22:40,067 --> 00:22:42,444
and she promised me she'd make some
when I took the medical licensing exam,

362
00:22:42,527 --> 00:22:44,488
but she passed two years ago.

363
00:22:45,072 --> 00:22:46,573
Okay, well, you should have it.

364
00:22:47,199 --> 00:22:49,618
You gotta stir the pot all night
to make the amount that we have here.

365
00:22:49,701 --> 00:22:51,244
You should try a little bit, at least.

366
00:22:51,912 --> 00:22:53,330
She must've really worked hard on it.

367
00:22:54,122 --> 00:22:56,333
She made it for him
with a lot of gratitude.

368
00:22:56,416 --> 00:22:58,251
So, you're a "gimme a thousand
paper cranes" type of guy?

369
00:22:58,335 --> 00:22:59,586
What?

370
00:23:00,170 --> 00:23:02,089
It's nothing,
just take care of those two, okay?

371
00:23:03,715 --> 00:23:04,716
Alright.

372
00:23:07,677 --> 00:23:09,846
RESUME

373
00:23:10,847 --> 00:23:13,475
I genuinely think that
it's justified to fire her right away.

374
00:23:13,558 --> 00:23:15,310
The level of disrespect
that that lady showed...

375
00:23:17,896 --> 00:23:21,108
I got the consent for the surgery
and updated his files and computer.

376
00:23:21,191 --> 00:23:22,192
Good work, thank you.

377
00:23:23,735 --> 00:23:25,487
- Dr. Do. Well?
- Hm?

378
00:23:25,570 --> 00:23:27,989
I got it. Take a read.

379
00:23:31,159 --> 00:23:32,494
"Gye Su-jeong."

380
00:23:32,577 --> 00:23:34,871
So that temp woman,
her name is Gye Su-jeong?

381
00:23:34,955 --> 00:23:37,040
Man, she looks like
she's older than I thought.

382
00:23:37,666 --> 00:23:39,209
She went to Cubanacan University

383
00:23:39,751 --> 00:23:41,002
and Florida College of Medicine.

384
00:23:41,670 --> 00:23:42,921
Look below that.

385
00:23:44,464 --> 00:23:47,926
She returned after doing volunteer work
in remote areas around the world.

386
00:23:48,593 --> 00:23:50,595
She holds a GS and CS, also...

387
00:23:50,679 --> 00:23:52,556
She's done quite a bit for her age,
I'll give her that.

388
00:23:53,140 --> 00:23:54,141
Wow, she's sick.

389
00:23:54,891 --> 00:23:58,770
Doctor Bae here is double-board certified
in both NS and GS, this is nothing.

390
00:24:00,313 --> 00:24:04,568
"After returning, registered with
Locum Tenens Agency as a general surgeon."

391
00:24:04,651 --> 00:24:08,155
And... "Hobby, surgery.
Special skills, surgery."

392
00:24:08,238 --> 00:24:09,865
She put surgery down for all her answers.

393
00:24:10,449 --> 00:24:11,700
Seems like a fraud.

394
00:24:11,783 --> 00:24:13,827
- You're sure you want her here?
- Do some more research.

395
00:24:13,910 --> 00:24:16,204
With that strong of a résumé,
why would she wanna freelance here?

396
00:24:17,664 --> 00:24:20,500
What's wrong with us, huh?
What's wrong with this hospital?

397
00:24:20,584 --> 00:24:23,003
That isn't what I meant to say...

398
00:24:27,507 --> 00:24:28,550
Hey, Gye Su,

399
00:24:32,220 --> 00:24:35,849
for the time being, assist Doctors Ma
and Park, that's where we need you.

400
00:24:43,273 --> 00:24:44,274
Doctor Su-jeong.

401
00:24:45,525 --> 00:24:46,526
Assist them with what, Doctor?

402
00:24:46,610 --> 00:24:47,527
What do you mean, with what?

403
00:24:47,611 --> 00:24:49,738
You're gonna follow these two
on their rounds.

404
00:24:49,821 --> 00:24:51,114
Let's start with prepping
for the conference.

405
00:24:51,615 --> 00:24:52,949
I think we're done.

406
00:25:00,665 --> 00:25:01,541
What're you gonna do with her?

407
00:25:01,625 --> 00:25:04,878
We're short on specialized surgeons.
It's free, so we'll keep her for the week.

408
00:25:05,712 --> 00:25:06,713
And because we're nice.

409
00:25:07,506 --> 00:25:09,716
Look, we'll just keep her at her desk
so Director Kim can't see her.

410
00:25:19,309 --> 00:25:21,728
SEO BYEONG-GYU, MALE/80 C24
MALIGNANT NEOPLASM OF BILIARY TRACT

411
00:25:30,612 --> 00:25:31,613
Sorry, I, uh...

412
00:25:33,949 --> 00:25:35,075
That inguinal hernia patient that day?

413
00:25:37,118 --> 00:25:39,371
I was at the pool hall with you.
Remember that?

414
00:25:40,747 --> 00:25:42,707
Man, your diagnosis that day was spot on,

415
00:25:42,791 --> 00:25:44,501
and thanks to you, he was able
to have a successful operation.

416
00:25:46,002 --> 00:25:49,297
Although, uhm...
how come at the end, you made an "X"?

417
00:25:49,381 --> 00:25:51,091
What do people draw an "X" to get across?

418
00:25:52,926 --> 00:25:54,219
Uhm, well...

419
00:25:54,719 --> 00:25:56,221
I guess to say, "no", or "can't be done"?

420
00:25:56,304 --> 00:25:57,681
Well, then you know.

421
00:26:00,767 --> 00:26:05,605
Meaning, "you... are not it."
Or, "you can't do anything"?

422
00:26:06,481 --> 00:26:08,441
So you don't think I have what it takes?
Wait, why, though?

423
00:26:08,525 --> 00:26:10,694
Why don't- Why don't I?
Why did you give me an "X"?

424
00:26:10,777 --> 00:26:13,488
I don't remember telling you to look
at Mister Seo Byeong-gyu's chart.

425
00:26:13,572 --> 00:26:15,031
He runs a rubber factory.

426
00:26:15,115 --> 00:26:18,159
That's right, we actually get our
surgical gloves from his factory, as well.

427
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:21,037
- He seemed very proud to be our supplier.
- Just do the work I assigned you.

428
00:26:21,121 --> 00:26:23,373
If you were him, would you want
the Director to operate on you?

429
00:26:23,456 --> 00:26:24,291
Huh?

430
00:26:24,374 --> 00:26:26,918
Well, you're a doctor too, so you know
this isn't the right thing to do.

431
00:26:27,002 --> 00:26:29,546
I consider that matter addressed
at the conference earlier.

432
00:26:29,629 --> 00:26:30,839
Then, would you want him to?

433
00:26:32,340 --> 00:26:33,842
- Yes, of course.
- Then...

434
00:26:36,469 --> 00:26:37,470
what if it were your parents?

435
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:40,849
If it wasn't you who needed surgery.
How about your mother?

436
00:26:40,932 --> 00:26:44,102
Uh, do- do we really
need to make it so personal?

437
00:26:44,185 --> 00:26:45,937
Because, as it happens,
this patient has a child, too.

438
00:26:47,147 --> 00:26:48,148
They're not just a doctor.

439
00:26:50,942 --> 00:26:52,068
I'd pick the Director.

440
00:26:52,611 --> 00:26:56,698
My mother would let Director Kim
operate on her, and as a matter of fact,

441
00:26:57,657 --> 00:26:59,868
say I was actually the patient
and had a child of my own,

442
00:27:00,577 --> 00:27:03,663
I'd feel all the more willing
for the Director to handle my operation,

443
00:27:03,747 --> 00:27:05,123
if anything,
for the sake of my child's future.

444
00:27:07,250 --> 00:27:10,420
Hey, can you clean up this chart quickly,
and send it back to me.

445
00:27:10,503 --> 00:27:12,339
- Ah, yes, sir. Will do.
- Hm.

446
00:27:13,381 --> 00:27:16,426
- What's going on?
- Doctor Bae, I'm so glad that you're here.

447
00:27:17,761 --> 00:27:20,347
This is exactly the reason
I don't like any of you people.

448
00:27:21,139 --> 00:27:23,183
What? What did you say?

449
00:27:23,266 --> 00:27:24,976
"You people"? What'd you say? Huh?

450
00:27:25,060 --> 00:27:29,189
- I think you must've misheard , Dr. Bae.
- He heard it right. That's what I said.

451
00:27:29,773 --> 00:27:31,107
- Hey.
- It's people like you...

452
00:27:32,776 --> 00:27:33,818
that I don't like at all.

453
00:27:36,321 --> 00:27:38,907
People who did nothing but study just
to make good money and get ahead.

454
00:27:39,866 --> 00:27:43,995
You're intelligent in the stupidest way,
with no convictions or ethics of your own.

455
00:27:44,079 --> 00:27:47,415
You grovel in front of attendings, but
hold your heads high in front of patients.

456
00:27:47,499 --> 00:27:50,085
You flatter your attendings,
but treat nurses like shit.

457
00:27:50,168 --> 00:27:53,421
You ignore corruption above you,
but say the system's why you're corrupt.

458
00:27:53,505 --> 00:27:55,256
You only care about your own convenience,

459
00:27:55,340 --> 00:27:58,510
you're fine entrusting
a patient's surgery to that dinosaur

460
00:27:58,593 --> 00:28:02,180
who can barely manage his own health
or keep his surgical skills up to date

461
00:28:02,263 --> 00:28:03,932
- you'd be lucky if he kept a steady hand.
- Hey, you shut your mouth, that's en-

462
00:28:04,015 --> 00:28:08,687
You complacent people, who despite knowing
the suffering the patient will undertake,

463
00:28:09,312 --> 00:28:13,733
that a life is at stake, turn a blind eye,
all you think of is how you get off easy.

464
00:28:13,817 --> 00:28:15,652
You people,
who think it's normal for patients

465
00:28:15,735 --> 00:28:18,446
even elderly patients,
to beg for a life-or-death surgery,

466
00:28:18,530 --> 00:28:20,782
while thanking you
for doing what you should.

467
00:28:21,908 --> 00:28:23,034
People...

468
00:28:23,702 --> 00:28:25,578
that aren't anything more than doctors.

469
00:28:26,454 --> 00:28:27,455
Yeah.

470
00:28:29,708 --> 00:28:30,875
You guys are the lowest of the low.

471
00:28:32,460 --> 00:28:33,837
What the hell is wrong with you?
Get out, right now!

472
00:28:33,920 --> 00:28:35,588
- I- I can-
- Get out.

473
00:28:36,172 --> 00:28:37,549
- Get out, I mean it!
- Get out!

474
00:28:38,383 --> 00:28:40,927
What are you looking at?
What's up, you wanna go? Huh?

475
00:28:42,053 --> 00:28:44,389
Fine, come at me.

476
00:28:44,472 --> 00:28:45,849
- Come, try me.
- Oh no, what is this?

477
00:28:47,475 --> 00:28:50,019
What? You gonna
throw that little sack? Huh?

478
00:28:51,229 --> 00:28:52,230
<i>Six o'clock!</i>

479
00:28:56,067 --> 00:28:57,235
Yeah, that's right.

480
00:28:57,318 --> 00:28:58,945
- Run away, get out!
- Oh.

481
00:29:00,447 --> 00:29:01,489
Why "oh"?

482
00:29:05,618 --> 00:29:07,120
What? Don't tell me...

483
00:29:09,664 --> 00:29:10,665
Did she just clock out?

484
00:29:12,167 --> 00:29:14,043
You, go get her back,
we gotta get her back, let's go.

485
00:29:14,127 --> 00:29:15,336
- Yes, sir.
- Bring her back here, right now.

486
00:29:16,254 --> 00:29:18,631
Damn it. Who's she think she is,
clocking out and walking out that way?

487
00:29:48,119 --> 00:29:49,829
ROOM 4210 SEO ******-GYU

488
00:30:00,173 --> 00:30:02,258
- My goodness. Oh my, just as I thought.
- Hello.

489
00:30:02,342 --> 00:30:04,803
I'm glad we picked the Director
to handle things.

490
00:30:04,886 --> 00:30:06,971
All the doctors have been
taking turns checking on us.

491
00:30:07,055 --> 00:30:09,140
- Oh, was another doctor here to see you?
- Yes.

492
00:30:09,224 --> 00:30:11,518
- Actually, it was just a little while ago.
- Ah.

493
00:30:11,601 --> 00:30:14,395
Here. Oh, here,
you should have some mango too.

494
00:30:15,814 --> 00:30:18,316
Our daughter got them for us
when she stopped by

495
00:30:18,399 --> 00:30:19,442
to perk up her dad,

496
00:30:20,568 --> 00:30:22,654
since he'll have to fast for his surgery.

497
00:30:22,737 --> 00:30:23,738
- Have some.
- It's extra sweet, so look out.

498
00:30:24,364 --> 00:30:27,158
The doctor who stopped by earlier
had some mango, and enjoyed it too.

499
00:30:27,700 --> 00:30:30,411
Mm, you gave the doctor
a little yogurt too, right?

500
00:30:30,495 --> 00:30:31,663
Yes, of course.

501
00:30:32,956 --> 00:30:35,375
Ah, actually, I think they
might've been a doctor.

502
00:30:35,458 --> 00:30:37,919
Did you see their name?
We have it on our coat.

503
00:30:38,002 --> 00:30:39,838
No, this doctor didn't
have their white coat on.

504
00:30:40,380 --> 00:30:41,548
Although, she said she was a doctor.

505
00:30:42,590 --> 00:30:44,509
- It was a woman, is what you're saying?
- That's right.

506
00:30:45,718 --> 00:30:48,429
Ah, it's just... she said something odd.

507
00:30:49,681 --> 00:30:53,434
- She said we should delay the surgery.
- Oh, well...

508
00:30:53,518 --> 00:30:55,937
Is Director Kim alright?
Is there anything that we should know?

509
00:30:56,020 --> 00:30:58,731
Oh, no, he's great! Uh, did she happen
to tell you a reason, or was that every-

510
00:30:58,815 --> 00:31:02,110
Oh, I said, "No,
because of the factory, we can't delay."

511
00:31:02,193 --> 00:31:05,530
Then she asked if I'd let
another doctor do the operation,

512
00:31:05,613 --> 00:31:07,282
I said, "I don't want anyone else.

513
00:31:07,365 --> 00:31:11,661
"I absolutely require Director Kim,
exactly as I'd picked, only he can do it."

514
00:31:11,744 --> 00:31:13,413
Ah... I think she was just curious.

515
00:31:14,622 --> 00:31:17,792
I can assure you, your surgery
will go great tomorrow.

516
00:31:17,876 --> 00:31:20,003
- Ah, well, alright. Thank you very much.
- Of course.

517
00:31:20,086 --> 00:31:21,212
Ah, thanks so much for this.

518
00:31:21,296 --> 00:31:22,547
- Of course.
- Rest up.

519
00:32:02,962 --> 00:32:04,756
- Let's try this first.
- Still,

520
00:32:05,423 --> 00:32:07,717
It's the largest hospital
in the Seoul metro area,

521
00:32:08,301 --> 00:32:09,928
but they're less meddlesome
than in Seoul itself.

522
00:32:10,011 --> 00:32:12,972
They're a little shadier, so it's easier
to squeeze money out of 'em,

523
00:32:13,056 --> 00:32:13,932
and for us, that's a win.

524
00:32:14,015 --> 00:32:16,476
I think you mean
it's a win for you, actually, huh?

525
00:32:18,102 --> 00:32:18,937
Su-jeong...

526
00:32:19,020 --> 00:32:20,939
you shouldn't forget to breathe
while you're eating.

527
00:32:22,357 --> 00:32:25,401
You should also be taking shorter showers.
The gas bill went up again.

528
00:32:25,485 --> 00:32:26,986
Well, I pay everything I owe.

529
00:32:30,031 --> 00:32:31,032
So, about the director.

530
00:32:31,449 --> 00:32:32,492
Who? Kim Myeong-seop?

531
00:32:32,575 --> 00:32:33,952
You know anything about him?

532
00:32:35,453 --> 00:32:37,789
You wanna know, I'll charge you.
It'll come out of your check.

533
00:32:38,373 --> 00:32:40,917
My goodness, you're as ruthless
as they say you are, aren't you?

534
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:42,085
And, hey, get some more in there.

535
00:32:44,879 --> 00:32:45,922
Hey, who cooked this?

536
00:32:48,049 --> 00:32:50,969
Director Kim, we would like to say sorry
that we're late sending our regards.

537
00:32:51,052 --> 00:32:52,345
There's no need to say sorry.

538
00:32:52,929 --> 00:32:56,057
Usually, we only give this to people
who sign a contract with us, but...

539
00:32:56,140 --> 00:32:59,102
Director Kim, allow us to
make our amends through this.

540
00:32:59,185 --> 00:33:04,857
Ah... is this... your signature gift?
Your famous melon box you gift to clients?

541
00:33:04,941 --> 00:33:07,610
Goodness, well, your recognizing it
is most appreciated.

542
00:33:09,237 --> 00:33:11,656
- I left its contents with your secretary.
- Ah, I see. Uh... mm...

543
00:33:15,076 --> 00:33:17,203
Uh... as you know, Mister Director,
you hold on to the box.

544
00:33:17,286 --> 00:33:18,287
Ah, okay... ah.

545
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:26,212
Ah, my goodness, this melon just looks
like the most delicious thing, eh?

546
00:33:26,295 --> 00:33:29,007
The best. I choose
the highest-quality melons, Director.

547
00:33:29,090 --> 00:33:30,842
It's imported as well,
so it's quite some trouble to get.

548
00:33:30,925 --> 00:33:31,926
I see.

549
00:33:33,344 --> 00:33:36,639
Now, Director, Doctor Gye Su-jeong
has spent many years outside of Korea.

550
00:33:37,223 --> 00:33:39,392
She's not used to Korean hospital culture.

551
00:33:39,475 --> 00:33:43,354
She acted out of turn because she's
unfamiliar with your illustrious legacy.

552
00:33:43,438 --> 00:33:44,605
Please give her another chance.

553
00:33:45,606 --> 00:33:46,441
All right.

554
00:33:46,524 --> 00:33:48,234
Doctor Gye has much
left to learn, I would say.

555
00:33:49,110 --> 00:33:52,280
Please, just keep her around
and have her do menial tasks.

556
00:33:52,363 --> 00:33:53,990
She just doesn't know
any better, that's all.

557
00:33:55,908 --> 00:33:58,369
I also will be coming to
see you operate today, as well.

558
00:33:58,453 --> 00:34:00,163
Oh... really?

559
00:34:00,246 --> 00:34:02,749
Yes, the MS technique would be amazing...

560
00:34:02,832 --> 00:34:04,584
to witness in an OR with my own eyes.

561
00:34:05,418 --> 00:34:06,419
Alright.

562
00:34:07,086 --> 00:34:08,087
I'll allow you to come.

563
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:09,881
Thank you, Director.

564
00:34:17,638 --> 00:34:19,807
I feel the need to say, it's been
a long time since he's held a scalpel,

565
00:34:19,891 --> 00:34:22,143
and there'll be
a million eyes watching this.

566
00:34:22,226 --> 00:34:23,186
I'll cover if he makes any mistakes.

567
00:34:23,269 --> 00:34:25,354
But without Director Kim knowing, got it?

568
00:34:25,438 --> 00:34:26,981
You got it. Understood, sir.

569
00:34:30,109 --> 00:34:31,402
Didn't Doctor Gye come in
to work this morning?

570
00:34:32,278 --> 00:34:34,697
Don't ask me that this early
ahead of an operation, it's bad luck.

571
00:34:34,781 --> 00:34:37,533
I didn't realize that simple
a question could be so touchy.

572
00:34:37,617 --> 00:34:38,826
You always have
to have the last word, don't you?

573
00:34:38,910 --> 00:34:41,662
Oh, I'll make sure you have the last word
as we keep working together.

574
00:34:41,746 --> 00:34:42,914
You know what you're doing, you little-

575
00:34:49,629 --> 00:34:51,506
Oh, Doctor, you're here!
We're so glad to see you.

576
00:34:51,589 --> 00:34:53,758
I heard Director Kim
asked you to attend today.

577
00:34:53,841 --> 00:34:55,134
It sure has been a while.

578
00:34:55,218 --> 00:34:56,844
It really is nice to see you, Doctor Bu.

579
00:34:57,345 --> 00:34:59,013
How d'you like it over there?
Surely you're doing well.

580
00:35:00,306 --> 00:35:02,850
I'm... just doing my best.

581
00:35:11,025 --> 00:35:12,026
Oh, you're also here.

582
00:35:17,949 --> 00:35:18,950
Well, what a shock.

583
00:35:19,450 --> 00:35:23,204
I mean, what a surprise Doctor Bu
blocked the time to watch the Director.

584
00:35:24,372 --> 00:35:27,917
I've heard stories that, supposedly,
he was to be the main hospital's Director,

585
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:31,963
but then he got passed over, after that
they put him in the south branch.

586
00:35:32,046 --> 00:35:34,799
How upsetting.
Gosh, how cruel, I had no idea.

587
00:35:35,925 --> 00:35:37,635
And, how come he was
passed over for Director?

588
00:35:38,219 --> 00:35:39,512
Well, he's no fun,

589
00:35:40,054 --> 00:35:42,265
and, to his credit,
way too good a doctor.

590
00:35:42,348 --> 00:35:44,600
In the Doctor community,
he's not the most well-liked among them.

591
00:35:44,684 --> 00:35:47,103
Hmm... mm.

592
00:35:47,186 --> 00:35:51,357
If I take your word for it, he's no fun,
I guess, more ways than just the one.

593
00:36:16,215 --> 00:36:18,593
No, not those. Bring me the powdered ones.

594
00:36:19,302 --> 00:36:21,262
- Sorry?
- Those make my hands sweat too much.

595
00:36:21,345 --> 00:36:22,889
Yes, we have them ready for you.

596
00:36:24,682 --> 00:36:25,683
Ah... right.

597
00:36:34,859 --> 00:36:38,404
Nothing of note happened during induction,
and his vitals are stable, Director.

598
00:36:52,168 --> 00:36:55,087
Finally, we'll have your
legendary surgery on record.

599
00:36:55,171 --> 00:36:57,340
Today's the first time
I've seen an upside to those cameras.

600
00:36:57,423 --> 00:36:59,342
There's no need to be nervous.

601
00:36:59,425 --> 00:37:02,303
I'll just do what I always do.

602
00:37:10,770 --> 00:37:12,146
That's Doctor Bae for you.

603
00:37:12,230 --> 00:37:14,023
Let me tell you, back in the day,

604
00:37:14,106 --> 00:37:17,902
I removed two gallbladders at once
listening to this, using my own technique.

605
00:37:17,985 --> 00:37:18,986
Turn up the volume.

606
00:37:21,155 --> 00:37:22,865
I can't hear the monitor, Director.

607
00:37:23,824 --> 00:37:24,825
Turn it down a bit.

608
00:37:25,451 --> 00:37:26,827
Okay... let's get started.

609
00:37:27,411 --> 00:37:29,580
We'll now begin the cholecystectomy
for Seo Byeong-gyu,

610
00:37:29,664 --> 00:37:31,290
performed by Director Kim Myeong-seop.

611
00:37:31,374 --> 00:37:32,708
- Let's do our best.
- Let's do our best.

612
00:37:42,551 --> 00:37:43,552
Scalpel.

613
00:37:48,849 --> 00:37:51,394
I swear, I warned him not to hand it
to the Director until he asked.

614
00:37:51,477 --> 00:37:54,647
Isn't it convenient to pass it to him
without him even needing to ask, though?

615
00:37:54,730 --> 00:37:56,941
No, he doesn't see it that way.

616
00:37:57,024 --> 00:37:59,277
For him, it’s a case of,
"How dare a mere nurse step out of line?"

617
00:38:00,069 --> 00:38:01,946
Back in his day,
he brought quite a few nurses to tears.

618
00:38:02,029 --> 00:38:03,531
What kind of asshole would do that?

619
00:38:03,614 --> 00:38:04,615
Ah, yes, I'm sure.

620
00:38:05,533 --> 00:38:06,951
I can certainly figure that he did.

621
00:38:08,286 --> 00:38:09,287
Do not.

622
00:38:12,665 --> 00:38:15,501
It's not too late to stop the operation
and take him for an MRI.

623
00:38:16,502 --> 00:38:18,296
What? Why would the patient need an MRI?

624
00:38:18,796 --> 00:38:20,381
No, not the patient. The Director.

625
00:38:20,965 --> 00:38:22,925
What kind of nonsense is this?
What're you on?

626
00:38:23,634 --> 00:38:24,719
You're gonna get kicked out,
like the conference?

627
00:38:24,802 --> 00:38:27,638
Oh, dear. Doctor Gye,
my goodness, you're rare today.

628
00:38:27,722 --> 00:38:29,223
Let's go over here, come here, Doctor Gye.

629
00:38:32,184 --> 00:38:33,185
Let it play out a little longer.

630
00:38:33,686 --> 00:38:34,895
This could be fun to watch, hmm?

631
00:38:45,698 --> 00:38:47,116
Who turned down the volume?

632
00:38:54,123 --> 00:38:55,124
Let's go, wipe already!

633
00:38:59,587 --> 00:39:00,588
MS forceps.

634
00:39:03,466 --> 00:39:07,511
These forceps here were designed
for the technique named after me.

635
00:39:07,595 --> 00:39:10,056
In my heyday, I used these to do
more than four surgeries a day.

636
00:39:10,139 --> 00:39:11,140
That's incredible.

637
00:39:11,223 --> 00:39:15,603
Mm. Once this surgery's done, I'll give
them to you to look after from now on.

638
00:39:15,686 --> 00:39:18,773
Oh, it would be an honor.

639
00:39:19,732 --> 00:39:23,611
Experienced surgeons arey able to handle
10 surgeries a day, in their prime.

640
00:39:23,694 --> 00:39:24,862
Well, he's slow as shit.

641
00:39:31,702 --> 00:39:32,703
Wipe.

642
00:39:38,209 --> 00:39:39,043
Look at this.

643
00:39:39,126 --> 00:39:42,213
As expected, severe adhesion
due to recurring inflammation.

644
00:39:42,296 --> 00:39:44,382
Opening him up was the right call, huh?

645
00:39:45,841 --> 00:39:48,844
Hmm.

646
00:40:14,453 --> 00:40:15,454
MS forceps.

647
00:40:19,208 --> 00:40:21,752
Look at this.
See how elegantly it grabs on.

648
00:40:22,253 --> 00:40:23,462
Right angle.

649
00:40:26,882 --> 00:40:28,050
Oh!

650
00:40:29,218 --> 00:40:31,053
What are you doing?
Sweat keeps getting in my eyes!

651
00:40:34,723 --> 00:40:35,808
Right angle.

652
00:40:36,851 --> 00:40:37,852
Metz.

653
00:40:42,940 --> 00:40:45,526
Blood pressure's dropping,
systolic below 60, heart rate's over 150.

654
00:40:45,609 --> 00:40:46,610
Vitals are unstable.

655
00:40:53,659 --> 00:40:54,994
He's in shock. I'll give him some fluids.

656
00:40:56,620 --> 00:40:57,997
- Director?
- Director, what should we...

657
00:40:59,498 --> 00:41:00,958
Dir... Director,
you need to pull your mask up.

658
00:41:02,418 --> 00:41:04,503
- Director?
- Director, are you okay?

659
00:41:04,587 --> 00:41:06,464
Director?

660
00:41:07,965 --> 00:41:09,175
- What's happening?
- Is he alright?

661
00:41:09,258 --> 00:41:11,302
Director! Director,
you need to wake up. Director!

662
00:41:11,385 --> 00:41:13,095
Director. Director?

663
00:41:13,179 --> 00:41:15,097
Squeeze my hand, sir. Squeeze my hand.

664
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:16,974
- <i>Is he alright?</i>
- Director's losing consciousness.

665
00:41:17,057 --> 00:41:18,893
It looks like he's paralyzed
on his left side!

666
00:41:18,976 --> 00:41:20,769
I suspect a CVA or a cerebral infarction.

667
00:41:20,853 --> 00:41:21,854
- Run a CT, now!
- Bring a stretcher!

668
00:41:21,937 --> 00:41:24,273
Vitals unstable. Risk of contamination.
Clear everything out now.

669
00:41:24,356 --> 00:41:26,984
Uh, secure an IV line for Director Kim,
and give him some fluids, hurry!

670
00:41:27,067 --> 00:41:28,402
Call neurosurgery!

671
00:41:28,486 --> 00:41:30,070
<i>No, wait, Doctor Bae, stay with him!</i>

672
00:41:30,154 --> 00:41:31,030
- <i>I'll be right there!</i>
- Okay!

673
00:41:31,113 --> 00:41:32,281
One, two, three.

674
00:41:32,364 --> 00:41:34,241
What are you going to do
about this patient? He's in shock!

675
00:41:34,325 --> 00:41:35,159
Get in here, quick!

676
00:41:35,242 --> 00:41:36,911
What are you going to do
about this patient?

677
00:41:36,994 --> 00:41:39,079
Doctor Bae Heung-gon, Doctor Ma Seong-gyu!

678
00:41:39,163 --> 00:41:40,998
- Come on, hurry, hurry, hurry!
- What are we supposed to do if you leave?

679
00:41:41,081 --> 00:41:42,416
Wait, what about the patient?

680
00:41:42,500 --> 00:41:44,043
You stay back here for now.
You take care of him.

681
00:41:44,126 --> 00:41:45,836
What? Where are you... Dr. Bae?

682
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:46,837
Ma Seong-gyu!

683
00:41:46,921 --> 00:41:51,300
Hey!

684
00:42:10,402 --> 00:42:13,280
Hey. Doctor Jo. Uh- w-what do we do?

685
00:42:13,364 --> 00:42:15,407
I'll keep him stable for now.
Go page someone.

686
00:42:15,491 --> 00:42:17,993
Everyone who wasn't scheduled
for surgery was in here,

687
00:42:18,077 --> 00:42:19,828
and they all just ran out of here
with the Director.

688
00:42:19,912 --> 00:42:20,913
There's nobody else available.

689
00:42:20,996 --> 00:42:23,791
Page anyway, get anyone at all.

690
00:42:29,380 --> 00:42:30,548
Should I give it a try?

691
00:42:31,048 --> 00:42:31,882
What?

692
00:42:31,966 --> 00:42:35,970
This patient is laying on this table,
fighting for his life, and he's all alone.

693
00:42:36,929 --> 00:42:39,557
I- Oh, I have to do something...

694
00:42:41,642 --> 00:42:43,852
No, but... uh, there's too many
different things here.

695
00:42:44,436 --> 00:42:46,564
You're just an intern,
you crazy son of a bitch!

696
00:42:46,647 --> 00:42:47,940
Call a resident or higher right now!

697
00:42:48,023 --> 00:42:50,067
There's no one else available,
there's nobody else...

698
00:42:54,863 --> 00:42:55,864
There is someone else.

699
00:43:23,517 --> 00:43:24,518
Vitals?

700
00:43:25,102 --> 00:43:27,187
Blood pressure undetectable,
heart rate 170.

701
00:43:29,023 --> 00:43:31,817
Alright, everyone, get ready to go.

702
00:43:31,900 --> 00:43:33,944
Put your hands up.

703
00:43:35,988 --> 00:43:37,781
I brought what you asked for.

704
00:43:37,865 --> 00:43:40,784
Everyone, switch to those gloves
and change into new surgical gowns.

705
00:43:40,868 --> 00:43:42,828
Turn up the ventilation
in the OR to the max.

706
00:43:42,911 --> 00:43:45,164
- Give him epinephrine and dex, stat.
- On it.

707
00:43:47,041 --> 00:43:48,250
You. Assist.

708
00:43:48,334 --> 00:43:49,335
Yes, ma'am.

709
00:44:04,099 --> 00:44:05,184
It stopped now.

710
00:44:09,938 --> 00:44:12,983
Turn off the music.

711
00:44:13,067 --> 00:44:15,736
BP is 120 over 65. Heart rate is 90.

712
00:44:28,207 --> 00:44:29,458
Resuming surgery.

713
00:44:30,417 --> 00:44:31,418
Tie 2-0 silk.

714
00:44:38,092 --> 00:44:39,093
Off.

715
00:44:41,178 --> 00:44:42,179
Scissors.

716
00:44:44,098 --> 00:44:45,099
Tie.

717
00:44:53,732 --> 00:44:54,733
Now off.

718
00:45:07,037 --> 00:45:08,080
Sponge forceps.

719
00:45:08,706 --> 00:45:09,707
Hold this.

720
00:45:10,374 --> 00:45:11,625
Forceps.

721
00:45:30,686 --> 00:45:31,687
Right angle.

722
00:45:32,855 --> 00:45:35,816
Now hand me whatever you think I need.
If I need something else, I'll ask.

723
00:45:35,899 --> 00:45:37,067
Understood, Doctor.

724
00:45:44,408 --> 00:45:45,534
Bile duct ligation.

725
00:45:46,160 --> 00:45:47,494
Her hands are quick, huh, Doctor?

726
00:45:51,331 --> 00:45:53,584
It's a pleasure to meet you,
my name is Jang Hui-suk,

727
00:45:53,667 --> 00:45:54,835
the head of Korea's
first locum tenens agency.

728
00:45:54,918 --> 00:45:56,295
DIRECTOR JANG Hui-suk LOCUM TENENS AGENCY

729
00:45:56,378 --> 00:45:58,756
I'll proudly say she's the agency's
most talented surgeon.

730
00:45:58,839 --> 00:46:02,134
The great Doctor Gye Su-jeong,
general surgeon.

731
00:46:12,269 --> 00:46:14,146
Specimen is out. Send it to pathology.

732
00:46:15,773 --> 00:46:16,774
What's the gauze count?

733
00:46:17,274 --> 00:46:18,817
The gauze count... looks correct.

734
00:46:20,527 --> 00:46:21,612
Let's close him up.

735
00:46:24,573 --> 00:46:26,533
SURGERY TIME, CURRENT TIME,
ANESTHESIA TIME

736
00:46:40,005 --> 00:46:41,590
Blood loss?

737
00:46:41,673 --> 00:46:43,634
- 200 cc.
- Before he wakes, inject hydrocortisone.

738
00:46:43,717 --> 00:46:45,677
Injecting 100 milligrams
of hydrocortisone.

739
00:46:49,473 --> 00:46:50,516
Let's wrap up.

740
00:47:37,145 --> 00:47:38,230
Doctor Gye Su-jeong.

741
00:47:41,441 --> 00:47:42,484
Thank you for your hard work.

742
00:47:47,072 --> 00:47:48,073
Thank you for your hard work.

743
00:47:49,658 --> 00:47:50,659
Thanks for your hard work!

744
00:47:51,034 --> 00:47:52,202
Thanks for your hard work!

745
00:48:06,091 --> 00:48:08,635
My goodness.
Doctor Bu, you're still in here?

746
00:48:09,219 --> 00:48:10,971
Oh, I even left my phone in here.

747
00:48:11,054 --> 00:48:12,055
I was so out of it.

748
00:48:14,933 --> 00:48:16,643
Director Kim is alright now.

749
00:48:16,727 --> 00:48:19,938
Our NS team, along with Doctor Bae,
are very good at what they do.

750
00:48:21,189 --> 00:48:22,107
Well, that's a relief.

751
00:48:22,190 --> 00:48:24,359
How on earth did that mad dog-
that Doctor Gye...

752
00:48:25,027 --> 00:48:27,321
I just don't get it.
It was like she could tell...

753
00:48:30,532 --> 00:48:32,200
What are you doing? Are you crazy?

754
00:48:32,284 --> 00:48:33,744
What'd you inject him with? Huh?

755
00:48:33,827 --> 00:48:35,579
Doctor! Look, look! He's breathing again!

756
00:48:37,164 --> 00:48:39,166
Get a move on. Open up his blood vessels.

757
00:48:50,302 --> 00:48:52,220
DIRECTOR JANG Hui-suk LOCUM TENENS AGENCY

758
00:49:35,722 --> 00:49:39,643
Doctor Gye!

759
00:49:53,740 --> 00:49:56,576
Okay, so... Doctor Gye Su-jeong
handled the operation, then?

760
00:49:57,327 --> 00:49:58,787
Did you page her?

761
00:49:58,870 --> 00:50:00,872
Are you trying to reprimand
Doctor Park Tae-gyeong right now?

762
00:50:01,415 --> 00:50:03,000
How is it not a problem
no one else was there?

763
00:50:03,083 --> 00:50:04,584
It was a very urgent emergency situation,

764
00:50:04,668 --> 00:50:07,045
it was a high-risk scenario where
another patient needed our attention--

765
00:50:07,129 --> 00:50:09,256
The Director clearly mattered more to you.

766
00:50:09,339 --> 00:50:11,216
How could you abandon
your current patient?

767
00:50:11,299 --> 00:50:12,926
What do you expect?
Are we supposed to abandon other patients?

768
00:50:13,552 --> 00:50:14,928
Isn't Director Kim our patient now, too?

769
00:50:15,012 --> 00:50:17,472
You should've left someone
behind to handle the surgery!

770
00:50:20,684 --> 00:50:22,436
Hold on!

771
00:50:29,443 --> 00:50:30,902
Doctor, what are you doing?

772
00:50:30,986 --> 00:50:32,946
Put that bowl down right now!

773
00:50:35,032 --> 00:50:38,702
Dr. Gye, you performed surgery without
permission to handle the operation.

774
00:50:42,581 --> 00:50:46,293
You witnessed everyone panic
when Mr. Seo Byeong-gyu went into shock.

775
00:50:46,960 --> 00:50:48,462
Right, it was from an "unknown cause"?

776
00:50:50,213 --> 00:50:51,214
I think you know the cause.

777
00:50:51,882 --> 00:50:53,675
You do know the cause, don't you?

778
00:50:53,759 --> 00:50:54,843
Can you answer me now?

779
00:50:58,346 --> 00:51:01,308
Stop eating that! Stop!
Give it a rest with the noodles.

780
00:51:07,481 --> 00:51:08,815
You were there.

781
00:51:09,900 --> 00:51:12,652
You were there, you were there.
What, you're all doctors, or am I wrong?

782
00:51:14,529 --> 00:51:15,530
Think about it.

783
00:51:15,614 --> 00:51:18,283
That injection..
it was epinephrine, wasn't it?

784
00:51:18,366 --> 00:51:20,160
EPINEPHRINE:
TREATMENT FOR ALLERGIC REACTIONS

785
00:51:20,243 --> 00:51:21,328
Why do you ignore me?

786
00:51:22,329 --> 00:51:23,497
Oh, what now?

787
00:51:24,289 --> 00:51:25,290
What?

788
00:51:26,208 --> 00:51:29,002
Why are you staring? Why are you
mad-dogging me with that look? Huh?

789
00:51:30,670 --> 00:51:31,755
<i>Six o'clock!</i>

790
00:51:34,007 --> 00:51:35,842
Again? Not again. No way.

791
00:51:37,094 --> 00:51:38,345
Was I standing under a clock again?

792
00:51:38,428 --> 00:51:40,889
- Go! Go and catch her, bring her back!
- Yeah, will do.

793
00:51:44,935 --> 00:51:46,520
An epinephrine injection?

794
00:51:47,437 --> 00:51:49,940
But Director Kim had an ischemic stroke,
so why would she give him that?

795
00:51:50,524 --> 00:51:52,150
When Su-jeong
was in the observation gallery,

796
00:51:52,818 --> 00:51:54,444
she wanted to have
an MRI done on the Director.

797
00:51:54,528 --> 00:51:55,529
She did?

798
00:51:57,322 --> 00:51:59,950
I think she knew that the Director
was gonna go down.

799
00:52:14,756 --> 00:52:16,550
ROOM 4210 SEO ******-GYU

800
00:52:19,511 --> 00:52:21,471
"Go and bring her back"? Yeah, right.

801
00:52:22,931 --> 00:52:25,142
You earned going home
early today, Doctor Gye.

802
00:52:30,939 --> 00:52:33,150
GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

803
00:52:33,233 --> 00:52:34,985
Doctor Do... Doctor Do.

804
00:52:35,068 --> 00:52:36,236
Yes, sir?

805
00:52:36,319 --> 00:52:38,989
Was it Doctor Gye... who did the surgery?

806
00:52:39,739 --> 00:52:41,825
Ah... he's asking if it was you
that finished the operation.

807
00:52:43,702 --> 00:52:44,411
Not again with the nodding.

808
00:52:44,494 --> 00:52:46,329
- Uhh...
- Yes?

809
00:52:46,413 --> 00:52:47,455
She did a good job,

810
00:52:47,539 --> 00:52:52,127
and as expected, applying the MS technique
was the right call.

811
00:52:52,210 --> 00:52:53,211
Ah. Okay.

812
00:52:54,462 --> 00:52:55,672
"Good work", he said.

813
00:52:55,755 --> 00:52:59,467
And, "As expected, the MS technique
after opening him up was the right call."

814
00:52:59,551 --> 00:53:01,845
Actually, no. As expected,
open surgery was a mistake.

815
00:53:01,928 --> 00:53:04,723
If you don't have anything else to relay,
I'll excuse myself.

816
00:53:05,223 --> 00:53:06,141
Dr. Gye!

817
00:53:09,519 --> 00:53:12,272
You're fired! You're... crazy!

818
00:53:15,650 --> 00:53:18,320
The Director says,
"You're fired", and "You're crazy."

819
00:53:18,403 --> 00:53:19,404
Did you catch that?

820
00:53:29,080 --> 00:53:31,541
So, what entices a doctor
who hates doctors to work here?

821
00:53:31,625 --> 00:53:32,792
I was just terminated.

822
00:53:33,293 --> 00:53:34,294
Now, I'm going home.

823
00:53:56,483 --> 00:53:58,151
No way, they fired her for that?

824
00:53:59,486 --> 00:54:00,779
Miss Ju-hye.

825
00:54:00,862 --> 00:54:03,156
But she saved that patient's life,
how could he just cut her loose like that?

826
00:54:05,200 --> 00:54:07,535
- Doctor, stop.
- Let's eat, no more about this.

827
00:54:08,578 --> 00:54:10,038
We said we'd come back once we were done.

828
00:54:10,121 --> 00:54:13,041
Any doctor who knows how to operate
could've pulled off the surgery.

829
00:54:13,124 --> 00:54:14,417
One-hundred percent, Sir.

830
00:54:16,002 --> 00:54:17,254
This one time during a lecture,

831
00:54:17,337 --> 00:54:20,715
the professor accidentally
played a surgery video at 1.5 times speed.

832
00:54:20,799 --> 00:54:22,050
Everyone thought it was hilarious,

833
00:54:22,133 --> 00:54:25,887
but now, it's not so funny if you see
someone operate faster than that for real.

834
00:54:25,971 --> 00:54:28,181
Hey, how many surgeries
have you even seen, huh?

835
00:54:28,265 --> 00:54:30,725
I can go through
a surgery that quick, too.

836
00:54:30,809 --> 00:54:31,810
- Oh, is that so?
- -Mmm.

837
00:54:32,394 --> 00:54:33,395
At that speed?

838
00:54:35,397 --> 00:54:37,190
Did you watch the recording
of the operation?

839
00:54:37,274 --> 00:54:38,817
Did you see us change our gloves?

840
00:54:38,900 --> 00:54:41,069
That's why I was called in,
it was because of the gloves.

841
00:54:41,152 --> 00:54:42,737
She said she wanted to use non-latex ones.

842
00:54:43,822 --> 00:54:45,282
- A latex... allergy?
- A latex allergy?

843
00:54:45,365 --> 00:54:46,574
Anaphylaxis.

844
00:54:46,658 --> 00:54:47,701
How did she know?

845
00:54:47,784 --> 00:54:50,161
I mean, the patient's pre-op questionnaire
didn't say anything about latex.

846
00:54:50,245 --> 00:54:51,329
The rubber factory...

847
00:54:52,580 --> 00:54:55,375
Not everyone who works around rubber, even
for years, gets a delayed-onset allergy.

848
00:54:55,458 --> 00:54:57,627
But there was an allergen
present that triggered a reaction.

849
00:54:57,711 --> 00:55:00,463
No, no, no, hold on a second.
So then, how'd she know?

850
00:55:02,507 --> 00:55:04,843
The Director had a cerebral infarction,
how could she've known?

851
00:55:06,386 --> 00:55:07,387
Hold on...

852
00:55:08,555 --> 00:55:10,724
Maybe she drugged him earlier?

853
00:55:12,350 --> 00:55:14,311
Look, just stop talking nonsense,
and finish eating.

854
00:55:14,394 --> 00:55:15,770
She's been fired already, we're done.

855
00:55:17,522 --> 00:55:21,735
How absurd that the doctor saying,
"She drugged the Director" is still here,

856
00:55:21,818 --> 00:55:23,862
while the doctor who saved a life
just gets tossed out.

857
00:55:23,945 --> 00:55:25,488
My goodness, this hospital is sideways.

858
00:55:25,572 --> 00:55:28,658
Okay, that's enough, just give it a rest.
We're already on thin ice.

859
00:55:28,742 --> 00:55:29,951
That allergy's why I can't be eating...

860
00:55:30,618 --> 00:55:32,579
any tropical fruits or anything like this.

861
00:55:45,175 --> 00:55:47,761
It's a relief to see that you're alright
and still with us, Director Kim.

862
00:55:47,844 --> 00:55:50,138
Yeah.

863
00:55:50,221 --> 00:55:52,223
Yes... I was there for the whole thing.

864
00:55:53,183 --> 00:55:54,476
In fact, I was incredibly worried.

865
00:55:55,477 --> 00:55:59,731
In the OR, it looked like nobody else
knew you were in anaphylactic shock.

866
00:55:59,814 --> 00:56:03,193
Anaphylactic shock? What, how'd you...

867
00:56:03,276 --> 00:56:05,820
Well, I stopped by your office
earlier this morning to say hi,

868
00:56:05,904 --> 00:56:07,989
and happened to see an old melon
your receptionist threw out.

869
00:56:09,199 --> 00:56:13,119
And during the surgery, I saw you keep
clawing at your neck, scratching an itch.

870
00:56:14,329 --> 00:56:15,372
And among medical professionals,

871
00:56:15,455 --> 00:56:20,001
a latex allergy surfacing later in life,
I wouldn't say it's uncommon, is it?

872
00:56:20,085 --> 00:56:21,336
What latex allergy?

873
00:56:21,419 --> 00:56:22,462
Oh, Director Kim.

874
00:56:24,506 --> 00:56:26,049
Why would you do something like that?

875
00:56:26,132 --> 00:56:28,885
Powdered gloves are banned in law.

876
00:56:28,968 --> 00:56:32,430
Powder can get in the respiratory system
and cause anaphylaxis, among other things.

877
00:56:34,057 --> 00:56:37,102
You ignored the risk nonetheless
for your own convenience, didn't you?

878
00:56:40,188 --> 00:56:42,524
While a patient's life was on the line,
in your hands.

879
00:56:42,607 --> 00:56:45,068
No, I- I didn't- I didn't know.

880
00:56:45,151 --> 00:56:46,903
Oh, but of course you didn't know.

881
00:56:46,986 --> 00:56:50,740
Because who could've known that either
of you had a latex allergy ahead of time?

882
00:56:52,033 --> 00:56:53,827
Or that you'd have a reaction?

883
00:56:56,079 --> 00:57:01,209
How many years have you been out of the OR
to not know something so simple?

884
00:57:02,961 --> 00:57:04,838
The recording doesn't show anything,
don't worry, sir.

885
00:57:05,463 --> 00:57:06,464
There's something else, though.

886
00:57:11,970 --> 00:57:13,805
Even though you left, these stayed behind.

887
00:57:25,233 --> 00:57:27,694
MAY EXACERBATE
LATEX-INDUCED ALLERGIC REACTIONS

888
00:57:27,777 --> 00:57:30,530
I also happened to hear the locum tenens
agency had given a gift box to you.

889
00:57:32,198 --> 00:57:34,492
The hospital still cut a check
to the temp doctor anyway,

890
00:57:34,576 --> 00:57:38,037
meaning this didn't cost you at all
and still managed to line your pockets.

891
00:57:40,957 --> 00:57:43,585
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

892
00:57:45,295 --> 00:57:46,463
Just keep breathing, don't worry.

893
00:57:48,506 --> 00:57:49,632
I only want one thing.

894
00:57:51,759 --> 00:57:52,760
A single, small request.

895
00:57:59,142 --> 00:58:01,936
- Thank you so much.
- Please get home safely.

896
00:58:03,229 --> 00:58:05,732
Okay, Doctor,
thank you for everything you've done.

897
00:58:16,826 --> 00:58:19,829
THE DIRECTOR WILL BE MAKING ROUNDS
PLEASE GET READY

898
00:58:27,795 --> 00:58:31,216
<i>Director Bu Seung-gwon</i>
<i>will now begin to make his rounds.</i>

899
00:58:35,220 --> 00:58:36,221
Sorry, excuse me.

900
00:58:57,408 --> 00:58:59,702
DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

901
00:59:08,419 --> 00:59:12,173
Thank you very much for requesting
Dr. Gye from our agency, Director.

902
00:59:12,257 --> 00:59:13,258
We're grateful to have been selected.

903
00:59:15,552 --> 00:59:16,553
Hold on, Director Bu...

904
00:59:17,095 --> 00:59:20,056
I'll hand this to you,
this is the new contract we've drawn up.

905
00:59:20,139 --> 00:59:21,140
Just a moment.

906
00:59:26,646 --> 00:59:27,814
EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT

907
00:59:27,897 --> 00:59:29,023
Wait, but...

908
00:59:31,651 --> 00:59:33,778
We'll be requiring an eight-hour workday,

909
00:59:33,861 --> 00:59:35,196
as well as compensation for overtime,

910
00:59:35,280 --> 00:59:37,240
extra pay per surgery performed,

911
00:59:37,323 --> 00:59:38,449
with nighttime surgeries
at twice the rate.

912
00:59:39,576 --> 00:59:41,160
Take a look at the rate list.

913
00:59:43,830 --> 00:59:44,872
So you're saying extra...

914
00:59:45,540 --> 00:59:46,541
Uh, at these rates...

915
00:59:47,125 --> 00:59:49,085
she would earn more than my salary.

916
00:59:50,044 --> 00:59:51,462
I can't accept this, Director Bu.

917
00:59:51,546 --> 00:59:54,173
Why not come work through
our agency as well, then, Doctor?

918
00:59:55,592 --> 00:59:58,094
Could I raise something? Director,
if she botches it when operating,

919
00:59:58,177 --> 00:59:59,596
we're the ones who'll end up being liable.

920
00:59:59,679 --> 01:00:02,807
Doctor Gye Su-jeong won't do any work
that doesn't require a medical license.

921
01:00:02,890 --> 01:00:04,267
No menial tasks.

922
01:00:04,350 --> 01:00:07,395
There're many smaller tasks to be done
that the hospital especially depends on.

923
01:00:07,478 --> 01:00:09,188
- That's the reason we hired you-
- Hold that thought.

924
01:00:09,772 --> 01:00:11,983
For example, assisting attendings
with their research projects.

925
01:00:12,066 --> 01:00:13,359
That is not something I do.

926
01:00:13,443 --> 01:00:14,611
Doing research for attendings' papers.

927
01:00:14,694 --> 01:00:15,612
That is not something I do.

928
01:00:15,695 --> 01:00:17,071
Director rounds, attending rounds.

929
01:00:17,155 --> 01:00:17,989
That is not something I do.

930
01:00:18,072 --> 01:00:20,950
Company dinners, socializing,
events, taking part in pleasantries,

931
01:00:21,034 --> 01:00:22,702
or talent shows, anything like that.

932
01:00:22,785 --> 01:00:24,037
That is not something I do.

933
01:00:24,120 --> 01:00:25,121
It's all written there, in the contract.

934
01:00:26,205 --> 01:00:27,498
SPECIAL TERMS

935
01:00:27,582 --> 01:00:29,417
Don't ever start to think...

936
01:00:30,376 --> 01:00:31,377
those are things I will do.

937
01:00:32,003 --> 01:00:33,129
What d’you expect to do, then?

938
01:00:33,212 --> 01:00:35,006
What matters here,
is that Doctor Gye Su-jeong...

939
01:00:35,089 --> 01:00:36,174
At no point will I allow...

940
01:00:38,259 --> 01:00:39,302
any surgery to fail.

941
01:00:44,015 --> 01:00:45,016
Uh, Director, one second, please?

942
01:00:45,099 --> 01:00:46,142
You can start here today.

943
01:00:46,726 --> 01:00:48,978
Thank you, Director.
You won't regret this decision.

944
01:00:51,439 --> 01:00:53,358
I'm looking forward to
working with you, Doctor Gye Su-jeong.

945
01:00:56,235 --> 01:00:59,572
Social pleasantries, when they occur,
are another thing I won't do.

946
01:00:59,656 --> 01:01:00,657
You little-

947
01:01:03,576 --> 01:01:05,787
Director. So, what I shared with you,
was it of good use to you?

948
01:01:07,288 --> 01:01:08,790
Ah... yes.

949
01:01:08,873 --> 01:01:10,875
Oh, then we'll settle
that some other occasion, Director.

950
01:01:12,752 --> 01:01:14,504
Now, have a good day, everyone.

951
01:01:14,587 --> 01:01:16,631
<i>If I ever become</i>

952
01:01:16,714 --> 01:01:19,050
<i>Become lonely</i>

953
01:01:19,133 --> 01:01:21,969
Uh, hold on. No, wait a minute!

954
01:01:27,975 --> 01:01:31,688
Director, she won't add anything to help
build or secure the future you envisioned.

955
01:01:31,771 --> 01:01:33,856
She boasts an impressive
and notable career.

956
01:01:33,940 --> 01:01:35,775
Beyond that, she'll be
of great help to the hospital.

957
01:01:35,858 --> 01:01:37,860
Oh, I mean, there are plenty
of doctors who also have-

958
01:01:37,944 --> 01:01:39,529
Did you watch the entire
recording of her surgery?

959
01:01:39,612 --> 01:01:40,613
I did.

960
01:01:41,864 --> 01:01:45,451
In all these years, not once have I seen
anybody with the amount of speed she has.

961
01:01:56,045 --> 01:01:58,047
I feel like someone else
should have this instead.

962
01:02:00,133 --> 01:02:03,136
Ahh!

963
01:02:03,219 --> 01:02:07,014
Why are we letting that snake back here?
What the hell is going on?

964
01:02:07,098 --> 01:02:08,099
This is driving me crazy.

965
01:02:17,984 --> 01:02:22,071
<i>She rebukes being part of</i>
<i>the pack and despises standing authority.</i>

966
01:02:25,908 --> 01:02:27,160
There's a strong possibility...

967
01:02:28,661 --> 01:02:31,038
she'll stop our whole structure
in its tracks completely.

968
01:02:33,791 --> 01:02:35,960
RESUME NAME: GYE SU-JEONG

969
01:02:36,043 --> 01:02:37,044
<i>Dr. Gye Su-jeong!</i>

970
01:02:41,299 --> 01:02:42,300
Ah, here you go.

971
01:02:43,676 --> 01:02:46,053
I noticed your name
hadn't been embroidered on it yet.

972
01:02:57,648 --> 01:03:00,067
I also know why now.
Melon. Isn't that right?

973
01:03:00,151 --> 01:03:04,071
When people with latex allergy eat fruit,
an allergic reaction can trigger.

974
01:03:23,174 --> 01:03:24,675
<i>He runs a rubber factory.</i>

975
01:03:25,635 --> 01:03:28,054
No, not those. Bring me the powdered ones.

976
01:03:28,137 --> 01:03:31,224
<i>The only weapons stored</i>
<i>in her arsenal are her medical license,</i>

977
01:03:31,307 --> 01:03:34,060
<i>and the surgical skills</i>
<i>that she sharpened from bare metal.</i>

978
01:03:34,143 --> 01:03:35,686
Dr. Gye Su-jeong!

979
01:03:37,480 --> 01:03:38,481
Gye Su-jeong!

980
01:03:39,607 --> 01:03:40,983
Give us an answer for once.

981
01:03:42,235 --> 01:03:43,236
Can't you hear us?

982
01:03:45,029 --> 01:03:46,405
I said can't you hear us?

983
01:03:47,490 --> 01:03:49,408
Hey, Snake Su-jeong! Snake Su-jeong!

984
01:03:49,492 --> 01:03:51,035
<i>Gye Su-jeong, general surgeon.</i>

985
01:03:52,161 --> 01:03:54,664
She can be easily gotten rid of
if she no longer meets our needs.

986
01:03:56,415 --> 01:03:59,210
We can just put her in the can with
all the other issues this hospital has.

987
01:04:01,629 --> 01:04:04,590
We'll let this play out a little longer,
we'll know soon enough.

988
01:04:12,223 --> 01:04:14,267
You said you hated it here.
Why did you come back?

989
01:04:15,101 --> 01:04:17,520
If you hate it so much, why'd you
become a doctor in the first place?

990
01:04:20,773 --> 01:04:21,816
<i>Also known as...</i>

991
01:04:23,109 --> 01:04:24,861
<i>Doctor X.</i>

992
01:05:04,275 --> 01:05:08,905
IN MEMORY OF KIM HYUN-I,
OUR CHERISHED COLLEAGUE

993
01:05:08,988 --> 01:05:11,908
DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

994
01:05:12,575 --> 01:05:15,036
- <i>"Mad dog"?</i>
- <i>You don't have the skills.</i>

995
01:05:15,119 --> 01:05:16,495
<i>Are we seriously working with her?</i>

996
01:05:16,579 --> 01:05:17,872
<i>She's so annoying.</i>

997
01:05:17,955 --> 01:05:19,332
<i>I don't want the operation.</i>

998
01:05:19,415 --> 01:05:21,667
- I object.
- Are you saying you can do it, Doctor Gye?

999
01:05:21,751 --> 01:05:23,836
<i>Just let me die!</i>

1000
01:05:23,920 --> 01:05:26,422
<i>You could die today, next week,</i>
<i>it makes no difference in the long run.</i>

1001
01:05:26,505 --> 01:05:29,133
<i>A surgeon who performs surgery</i>
<i>no matter what danger a patient may be in.</i>

1002
01:05:29,216 --> 01:05:30,426
<i>Now, this is more like it.</i>

1003
01:05:30,509 --> 01:05:32,887
<i>You can't go on forever</i>
<i>and never fail an operation.</i>

1004
01:05:32,970 --> 01:05:34,513
<i>You're a doctor!</i>

1005
01:05:34,597 --> 01:05:36,182
<i>You should look after</i>
<i>your patient until the end!</i>
